{"parentUuid":"4fcbc5d0-953f-489a-bf4d-bfed1886bc1c","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"8caa67d2-997c-4b7f-ab12-8ec84fe807a8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ad03678","slug":"snug-orbiting-fountain","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01YRi6xtCyrozmSLxH35WnfF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google cluster trace 2011 task events schema columns timestamp job ID task index event type\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace based on Resource Usage\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270593953_Analysis_and_Clustering_of_Workload_in_Google_Cluster_Trace_based_on_Resource_Usage\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces v3\",\"url\":\"https://02075833655549046200.googlegroups.com/attach/610d690a6080d/Google%20cluster-usage%20traces%20v3_gg.pdf?part=0.1&vt=ANaJVrHfb6UNfEkB9bJDwvmIv8cURDKKuLYyifyQPsC6cgtqAS9PAdx6lFNiVeIvTSrvQn0mSXT_u7-dvC4AJQXVo4_9_JVyjZKEp3RoHLJiJU9vvNBqu3A\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about the Google cluster trace 2011 task events schema. Here's what I found:\n\n## Google Cluster Trace 2011 - Task Events Schema\n\nThe task event CSV files contain the fields: 'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'.\n\n### Key Column Details:\n\n**Core Identification Fields:**\n- Each record has a timestamp, which is in microseconds since 600 seconds before the beginning of the trace period, and recorded as a 64 bit integer\n- Tasks are identified by the job ID of their job and a 0-based index within the job\n\n**Event Type Information:**\n- Each job and task event has a value representing the type of event. The state of the job or task after the event can always be determined from this event type\n\n**Additional Schema Information:**\n- This table is represented by thirteen columns which include fields such as time stamp, missing information, index of tasks, event type, priority of a task which can be free priorities or a production priority\n\nThe trace comes from clusterdata-2011-2 trace starts at 19:00 EDT on Sunday May 1, 2011 and includes six principal CSV tables: machine events, machine attributes, job events, task events, task constraints, and task (instance) resource usage.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3013c5fa-2f9