{"parentUuid":"2edb0811-7f88-4426-ab1f-343cbca5803e","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"8caa67d2-997c-4b7f-ab12-8ec84fe807a8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ad03678","slug":"snug-orbiting-fountain","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Nj8tVT3qrifzUN66M7SHr9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Google cluster trace\" \"event type\" SUBMIT value 0 1 2 3 4 5 schema\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"谷歌集群数据分析clusterdata-2011-2_google cluster trace shujuji-CSDN博客\",\"url\":\"https://blog.csdn.net/snowleafzf/article/details/84203279\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Google cluster trace event types and their schema:\n\nIn the Google cluster trace dataset, the event types for jobs and tasks are defined as: 0.submit, 1.schedule, 2.evict, 3.fail, 4.kill, 5.finish, 6.lost, 7.update_pending, 8.update_running.\n\nThe search results show that this is part of the clusterdata-2011-2 trace dataset, which contains cell information of about 29 days from May 2011 on a cluster of about 12.5k machines.\n\nThe schema includes these event type values (0-5 that you specifically asked about):\n- **0**: SUBMIT - when a job/task is submitted\n- **1**: SCHEDULE - when a job/task is scheduled\n- **2**: EVICT - when a job/task is evicted\n- **3**: FAIL - when a job/task fails\n- **4**: KILL - when a job/task is killed\n- **5**: FINISH - when a job/task finishes\n\nAdditional event types beyond 0-5 include 6 (lost), 7 (update_pending), and 8 (update_running).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6818efc2-3f7c-4841-9d27-50b0fe0721d3","timestamp":"2026-01-29T04:50:23.086Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2edb0811-7f88-4426-ab1f-343cbca5803e"}
