 me search more specifically for the schema.csv file or the exact job events table column specification.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google 2019 Cluster sample\",\"url\":\"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/derrickmwiti/google-2019-cluster-sample\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/TraceVersion1.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/TraceVersion1.md\"},{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I have found information about the Google cluster trace dataset and its schema. Let me compile the information about the job events table schema columns and their field order:\n\n## Google Cluster Trace Job Events Table Schema\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the **Google cluster trace job events table schema**. Here's what I can tell you about the columns and field order:\n\n### Job Events Table Fields\n\nThe job events table contains fields like timestamp, a field in missing information, type of event, a scheduling class which represents latency sensitivity of a job or task, name of job which is mostly unique and generated in a hashed format.\n\n### Field Order and Description\n\nFrom the documentation, the typical column order for the job events table includes:\n\n1. **timestamp** - event timestamp, which is always stored in the first column\n2. **missing info** - Records without missing data have no value (empty string) in the \"missing info\" field.\n3. **job ID** - Unique identifier for the job\n4. **event type** - Each job and task event has a value representing the type of event. The state of the job or task after the event can always be determined from this event type.\n5. **user** - Username (hashed for confidentiality)\n6. **scheduling class** - Represents latency sensitivity of the job\n7. **job name** - Logical name of the job (hashed)\n8. **priority** - a small integer that is mapped here into a sorted set of values, with 0 as the lowest priority (least important).\n\n### Data Format\n\nIf there is no value for a field, then the field will be empty (no quotes). Boolean fields are represented as 0 (false) or 1 (true). All fields have been normalized so they do not contain commas, newlines(no content)Each dataset includes six principal CSV tables: machine events, machine attributes, job events, task events, task constraints, and task (instance) resource usage.\n\nThe official schema documentation is available in the v2.1 format + schema document referenced in the ClusterData2011_2 trace.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8e847e3a-fc52-403e-bc02-5edac2